WEBVTT

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:55.570
It’s been three days since I started working as a bodyguard here.

00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:58.400
It’s all thanks to Yaichi-dono for putting in a good word.

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:01.380
How long are you going to be eating?

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:03.680
Seriously...

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:08.370
Just take your time, Sensei.

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:09.420
But...

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:11.820
Master is very strict.

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:14.420
However, the old master was very proud of him.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:17.060
Even the neighbors praise him for being a suitable heir.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:22.690
If his wife would just deliver a child, everything would be perfect.

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:27.270
There’s nothing wrong here.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.610
It hasn’t been that long since our last job.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.000
Is it safe for us to proceed?

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:45.200
Don’t worry.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:49.490
Matsu is investigating our next prey thoroughly.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.680
After all, this was Ichi-san’s idea.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.530
I’m not sure about this...

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:58.460
You’re just not satisfied unless you complain about something, right, Ume?

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:04.430
Our next prey is the rice wholesaler Oomiya in the Saga District.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:05.930
We’ll abduct the owner.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:08.570
Is Masa going to help as well?

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:11.930
I’ve heard they’re looking for a bodyguard.

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:14.360
We’ll smuggle Masa in there.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:18.830
Will they even hire him?

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:21.590
Matsu is making the arrangements.

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:25.150
You’re such a great help, Matsu.

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.280
Why haven’t you called Masa here?

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:32.710
If he’s a part of this plan, he should be here.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:38.790
He won’t participate if we tell him what he’s doing.

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:41.430
I’ll explain it to him later.

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:46.950
We’ll get him involved steadily, huh?

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:59.520
You didn’t have to walk me home.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:01.070
I won’t let Matsu do it.

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:06.440
Ichi-san, is it really necessary to smuggle the ronin in there?

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:10.200
It’s not to spy on them.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:13.190
That is your job.

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:17.480
They will bring the bodyguard to the exchange.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:24.170
If it’s him, we won’t have to worry about anything, right?

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:30.540
And as Ume said, I want him to be an active participant in this job.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:39.780
Welcome.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:41.160
The lady is waiting for you.

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:47.720
Akitsu Sensei.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.070
Yes?

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:51.480
Ah, Matsukichi-dono.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:56.440
Matsukichi-san makes hairpins and tobacco pipes for the lady.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:58.830
She summons him quite often for his services.

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:02.270
Akitsu-san and I are friends with a certain person.

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:04.270
I see.

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:08.130
How is he doing?

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:13.670
Unlike the other swordsmen, he’s very kind.

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:17.250
But I heard his skills are impressive.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:21.220
Bye.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:30.370
He always ignores me at Ume-dono’s place.

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:32.690
I thought he had something against me.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.450
He might be a pretty nice guy.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.540
Is this a neighbor’s kid?

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:58.080
He hates me after one look.

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:10.010
The master must hate me, too.

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:15.680
Honorable Samurai, does your tummy hurt?

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:23.910
I see. You’re afraid of samurai.

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:27.650
I thought all of them were scary,

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:29.950
but I’m not afraid of you.

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:31.950
N-Not even a little?

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:33.530
Hey.

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:37.400
Will you be friends with me?

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:41.100
I’m Yuutarou.

00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:44.390
My name is Akitsu Masanosuke.

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:54.320
Is that you, Matsu?

00:06:56.920 --> 00:06:59.620
Did you infiltrate Oomiya?

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:03.300
No, I just did my regular visit as a craftsman.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:05.300
Did you see Masa?

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:07.710
He was playing with a kid.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:09.440
With a kid, huh?

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:13.840
When will you talk to him about this job?

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:19.880
I’ll tell him to head to Ume’s place once he returns to Nagaya.

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:22.240
I’ll tell him then.

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:35.240
Edo is a fine place for having so much polished rice.

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:50.610
Sensei! I told you not to enter the backyard.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:53.910
I was just patrolling.

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.410
Sorry.

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:01.340
Masa!

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:04.430
Yuutarou-dono.

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:05.710
Let’s play.

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:06.630
Sure,

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:09.400
but why are you inside the mansion?

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:11.400
I’m going to the river.

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:16.730
Oh, my. I didn’t expect him to get attached to a bodyguard.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:22.050
He seems to be bored since everyone is busy and can’t play with him.

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:25.310
Please play with him, okay?

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:26.550
Okay.

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:32.000
So, he’s the son of a maid.

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:38.700
Oh, yeah. I remember maids bringing their kids to work back at my old estate.

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:41.220
Masa!

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.610
Say, do you have siblings?

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:49.690
I have a younger brother and a sister in my hometown.

00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:53.280
I want a younger brother, too!

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:56.700
So, do you get along with your brother?

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:01.210
No, not really.

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:05.280
How is your job as a bodyguard going?

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:07.940
So far, so good.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:12.750
The shop is doing well, and I hope to be of use to them.

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:17.950
Oh, yeah. I heard you do bodyguard duty for a brothel.

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:20.790
I’m just freeloading.

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:26.900
Once you’re done with this job, I’ll refer you to Katsuraya.

00:09:27.410 --> 00:09:28.810
To that brothel?

00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:34.990
Thanks, but I’ll decline. I’d like to continue working for Oomiya.

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:37.620
Well, our next victim is Oomiya.

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:41.070
We’ll abduct their master.

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:46.900
But there doesn’t seem to be anything wrong there.

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:49.790
I told you that I’m not interested in any chivalry.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:56.280
We target dysfunctional families so that nothing can be traced back to us.

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:59.340
Oomiya is pretty wicked, too.

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:03.290
If we just blackmail them, they will kill us.

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:06.420
Well, they just happen to be merchants.

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:09.310
Usually, we go after the vassals of shoguns.

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:11.280
They wouldn’t dare report something like that.

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:16.800
What’s your objective?

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:18.670
Money.

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:20.010
Money?

00:10:21.380 --> 00:10:26.540
Everyone has their own circumstances. Just like you.

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:39.990
Akitsu Masanosuke dono

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:43.500
Just when I thought I had found a good job...

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:46.100
The rice is so expensive, isn’t it?

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:48.390
Yes, all I’ve been making is gruel.

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:49.920
Same here.

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:55.980
I had hoped to send them money that I earned legally...

00:10:56.680 --> 00:11:00.850
Anyway, I have to earn some money.

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:09.370
Masa-san.

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:11.090
Okinu-dono,

00:11:11.090 --> 00:11:13.060
those look heavy.

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:15.660
Let me carry them.

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:17.060
It’s okay.

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:22.480
You’re so kind, Masa-san.

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:27.030
Dad, I got the boards.

00:11:27.030 --> 00:11:29.400
Didn’t I tell you I’d get them?

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:31.420
Masa-san carried them.

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:35.550
Masa, come up. Ichi is here as well.

00:11:35.550 --> 00:11:36.300
Okay.

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:38.390
Thanks, Masa-san.

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:40.890
Watch your step.

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:48.130
I said...

00:11:48.130 --> 00:11:49.700
How did you fall now?

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:52.160
Where’s Ichi-san?

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:52.900
He’s upstairs.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:55.040
Hey, Masa!

00:11:56.210 --> 00:11:57.360
Wake up!

00:11:57.930 --> 00:11:59.150
And?

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:02.140
I’ve been summoned by Oomiya.

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:04.370
I was about to visit the lady now.

00:12:04.750 --> 00:12:05.660
What about her husband?

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:09.640
It’s harder to approach him than I thought.

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:12.690
Perhaps it’s better to watch things for a bit longer.

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:14.260
Yeah.

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:19.070
This is bad.

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:22.870
I just can’t remain calm.

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:27.350
The dumplings here are delicious, Mr. Leaf-picker.

00:12:29.130 --> 00:12:32.150
What is it this time? Waiting for a woman?

00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:34.150
No...

00:12:38.420 --> 00:12:42.520
You don’t look like a bodyguard at all.

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:46.960
One of the bath staff at my house has quit his job.

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:50.480
How about working for me? I’ll pay you well.

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:58.630
The fact that you aren’t enraged by that makes it hard for me to believe you’re a samurai.

00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:02.140
I’m Yagi.

00:13:02.140 --> 00:13:02.750
What’s your name?

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:04.840
Akitsu.

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:08.520
Come on. I was just pulling your leg.

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:12.600
Besides, I’m not rich enough to hire bath staff.

00:13:12.990 --> 00:13:14.560
Here are your dumplings.

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:16.840
I’m the third son of a shogun’s vassal.

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:18.680
I’m just living off the main family.

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:21.970
Anyway, have some dumplings.

00:13:26.750 --> 00:13:30.450
Matsukichi-san, I’m quite irritated.

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:35.860
I know it’s my fault that I can’t get pregnant,

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:44.980
but when the kid is laughing and screaming with the maid or the bodyguard,

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:47.140
I really get annoyed.

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:53.750
At first, I thought adopting was the only option, too.

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:55.170
Adopting?

00:13:55.170 --> 00:14:00.010
Besides, it’s the kid of my husband’s mistress.

00:14:00.010 --> 00:14:02.040
And now I get to raise that little bastard.

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:04.360
I’m losing my composure.

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:05.600
You mean Yuutarou?

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:08.640
Yeah.

00:14:09.020 --> 00:14:10.870
He’s not the son of the maid?

00:14:11.300 --> 00:14:13.490
He’s the adopted son.

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:17.090
To relieve stress, I have to waste money.

00:14:17.650 --> 00:14:23.710
Make a hairpin so expensive it will make my husband’s jaw drop, Matsukichi-san.

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:30.290
Hey, Masa. Over here.

00:14:34.030 --> 00:14:36.260
Rice cakes?

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:38.070
Here, take this.

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:40.770
Take the kid out and have him eat it.

00:14:41.510 --> 00:14:42.940
That’s nice of you.

00:14:51.020 --> 00:14:55.190
I wonder if he heard about the change in plans?

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:56.160
No idea.

00:14:58.390 --> 00:15:03.620
I’m amazed that Matsu missed the fact that the kid is the adopted heir.

00:15:04.910 --> 00:15:10.670
Didn’t I say he isn’t that much of a big shot?

00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:19.140
Yay! Rice cakes!

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:26.330
Delicious!

00:15:26.850 --> 00:15:28.310
Masa, you should eat one!

00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:29.960
Okay...

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:32.050
I’ll have some, too.

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:53.420
Geez, what a pain.

00:15:58.940 --> 00:16:01.480
This letter from the band called “Five Leaves” reads:

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:07.480
“Make the bodyguard who was with the kid when we kidnapped him deliver the money.”

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:12.700
The same bodyguard who passed out while trying to protect him...

00:16:13.850 --> 00:16:17.160
Don’t worry. They’ll give him back.

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:21.420
You can talk this easily because he’s not your own child!

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:25.140
You’re right. He’s not my child.

00:16:25.140 --> 00:16:27.120
I can’t believe you!

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:30.550
I’ll go then.

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:39.840
Hey.

00:16:44.590 --> 00:16:45.940
Matsukichi-dono.

00:16:46.410 --> 00:16:47.970
From the roof?

00:16:47.970 --> 00:16:50.160
No one followed you from Oomiya.

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:52.740
Go to Ume’s place.

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:02.000
You’re part of the Five Leaves?

00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:05.630
Ichi-san didn’t tell you?

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:09.550
I wanted to keep it quiet for a bit longer.

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:10.800
Why?

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:12.700
That made it all the more interesting.

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:17.570
Matsu used to be a robber who worked alone.

00:17:17.570 --> 00:17:20.460
That’s why he’s good at breaking into houses.

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:25.170
And I thought the old man was the fifth member.

00:17:26.630 --> 00:17:30.870
Anyway, you did a great job.

00:17:30.870 --> 00:17:32.430
Why are you depressed?

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:34.210
Because of so many things...

00:17:34.930 --> 00:17:37.410
The kid is safe at the old man’s place.

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:42.070
Have some rice cakes and cheer up.

00:17:44.070 --> 00:17:47.030
This was an easy job.

00:17:47.030 --> 00:17:48.360
Thanks to Masa.

00:17:49.230 --> 00:17:51.470
He was very useful.

00:18:06.700 --> 00:18:09.350
Are you going to collect the money?

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:18.620
This isn’t kidnapping.

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:20.230
Listen, kid.

00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:23.710
It looks like a kidnapping, but we’re really going to kill you.

00:18:23.710 --> 00:18:24.610
What?

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:27.200
Bro! You’re going to tell him?

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:32.660
The letter saying that you were kidnapped should have reached your home by now.

00:18:32.660 --> 00:18:35.760
But we didn’t send that.

00:18:36.710 --> 00:18:40.040
Someone else prepared all this.

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:43.740
We will just get paid for helping out.

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:47.350
Someone in your family planned this “kidnapping.”

00:18:47.750 --> 00:18:48.920
It’s a farce.

00:18:53.970 --> 00:18:56.810
Why do you have to make it look like a kidnapping?

00:18:58.370 --> 00:19:00.500
In order to deceive the master.

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:06.450
So, my mother planned this.

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:08.260
Right.

00:19:08.950 --> 00:19:12.450
When I threatened the guy who approached us, he told me everything.

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:15.800
Why did you accept his offer?

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:18.780
The boss of this turf asked us.

00:19:18.780 --> 00:19:20.490
We cannot decline it.

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:22.420
Besides, we need that money.

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:28.740
He said that the master was suspicious about this, too.

00:19:28.740 --> 00:19:30.920
Yet he didn’t try to stop it,

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:34.190
which means they don’t want you.

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:34.980
Ryu!

00:19:35.560 --> 00:19:38.410
We’re going to kill him anyway. Who cares?

00:19:39.350 --> 00:19:41.420
I’m not going to kill him.

00:19:41.420 --> 00:19:43.420
I dislike pointless bloodshed.

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:50.320
I’ll give them your topknot and blood-stained kimono as well as your swords.

00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:54.330
Once I get the money, you will be free.

00:19:54.650 --> 00:19:58.550
We’ll have to leave Edo anyway.

00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:00.080
I’ll come with you.

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:01.030
Me too.

00:20:01.480 --> 00:20:02.470
Will you come with us as well?

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:08.130
You have no other place to go.

00:20:09.360 --> 00:20:10.920
I’ll go back home.

00:20:11.530 --> 00:20:12.830
They’re going to kill you.

00:20:13.530 --> 00:20:18.060
I’ll go home! Yaichi’s there.

00:20:18.060 --> 00:20:19.570
Who’s Yaichi?

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:21.570
A servant.

00:20:22.180 --> 00:20:25.570
He will protect me.

00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:28.230
Yaichi, huh?

00:20:28.230 --> 00:20:33.000
The name of the guy who approached us was Yaichi.

00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:38.280
He seemed to be a servant.

00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:40.280
It was probably him.

00:21:08.940 --> 00:21:16.140
I’ve got a feeling that something was hidden

00:21:16.140 --> 00:21:25.430
in the words you once told me. Those words cross my mind again and again.

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:33.850
Yet your voice always sounds the same as before.

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:40.900
Every time I breathe, I wanna hold you in my arms

00:21:41.300 --> 00:21:49.830
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:21:50.670 --> 00:21:57.910
Every time I breathe, I just wanna hold you in my arms again

00:21:59.030 --> 00:22:06.730
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:22:07.390 --> 00:22:14.970
Every day I need you  All the time I'll be there for you

00:22:15.700 --> 00:22:24.080
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:22:30.400 --> 00:22:33.200
Next time on House of Five Leaves:

00:22:33.470 --> 00:22:34.570
Yagi here.

00:22:34.570 --> 00:22:37.950
It has been pretty tranquil out there.

00:22:37.950 --> 00:22:42.000
Once I’m done with work, it’s up to me to decide what to do!

00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:46.340
This world has become an easy-to-live place for people like me.

00:22:46.340 --> 00:22:48.010
Well then, the next episode’s title is:

00:22:48.010 --> 00:22:49.930
“Getting Carried Away.”
